-347e-5cb7-8b9b-0077208b27ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-331055" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}$ given $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nLet $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ=A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t}={{field-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}=L\\{A(t)\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={A}^{′}(t)\\text{ }dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ $0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-5}}\\,\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n." :question/worked-solution "Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ & =A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =A(t)-A(0) \\\\  & =A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ\\} & =L\\{A(t)\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & \\,⇒\\, & du={A}^{′}(t)\\,dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A(0)=0$ and $\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ we have $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0$ and\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3d0c888a-3aaa-5726-be27-ccbba915b7d5"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506620 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506597 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035e774f-669c-5e7b-97ae-98fe6b741631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}{A}^{″}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505920} {:answer/id #uuid "1b7ab260-ce33-585b-a3df-d2391101dca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}A(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505960} {:answer/id #uuid "26f6c02c-7b68-5ee3-b99a-35ad02706372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "sF(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505976} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5f8fa8-5e89-5519-868a-fda205012175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506096}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506096} :answer-field/id #uuid "09a061c0-a394-598e-a30e-f9f916c35a0f" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef0afb0-0e9f-593c-b760-f